book.page:
{{C|A Copyist's Declaration}}

Set down by Neseva Cask-Hand, clerk of the Open Basin fellowship, in
Uru Ux of 1000 AR.

Among our fellowship we teach that a place may begin when someone stops
walking, another stops beside them, and the two share water. We call
that chosen beginning the First Water. Other places began otherwise;
this is the beginning we offer to people who choose our rite.

{{K|[A different hand has crowded the gutter: "A custom is not a
history. Keep the basin if it serves you, but do not pour it backward
over everyone who came before."]}}
